Each line lists 3 glyphs with their possible meanings separated by '/'. Meanings separated by '/' are unrelated and context disambiguates. A glyph may have multiple functions (noun, verb, adjective, particle). When a glyph is used as a grammatical particle, its other meanings are ignored.

